{
  "requirement": "An application-supplied assessment procedure can perform ordinary computation\nand request zero or more typed model answers. It can use intermediate answers\nin later computation and requests, then return its `Criterion::Ok` value.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.procedures`. Each obligation maps to a marked test:\n\n- **Two typed requests, with an intermediate answer reused (`runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls`).**\n  - The `Memory::run_review` helper, with `ask_in_callback`, first asks a typed `Answer` about the current node's contents.\n  - It then computes a new context string from `first.n` and makes a second typed request with it.\n  - The test asserts `requests.len() == 2` and that `requests[1].0 == \"Check intermediate result 7\"`. This shows the first answer fed both ordinary computation (`format!`) and a later request.\n- **Return of the `Criterion::Ok` value (same test).** The procedure's returned assessment is checked with `assert!(value.output().result)`. It is then stored and its dependencies are asserted.\n- **Zero model requests (`caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly`).**\n  - Node 9 runs the procedure without any agent. The test asserts `!value.output().result`, so the returned value is checked in the false case too.\n  - It also asserts `state.reads.is_empty()` and `state.selections.is_empty()`.\n  - The procedure computes and returns its result without a model call.\n- **Several requests in one procedure, independent of each other (`shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls`).**\n  - Two typed asks go through a shared context. The test asserts their distinct typed results (7 and 11) and that two requests were made.\n  - A barrier forces the two asks to be in flight at once, so the test proves more than sequential calls.\n\nThe remaining clauses are \"ordinary computation\" and \"typed\" answers. Both are covered by the `format!` over `first.n` and the typed `Answer` results. I found no uncovered obligation or boundary, and I found no {fixme} acknowledgments.",
